{"id":"CVE-2018-0487","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"debian","published":"2018-02-13T15:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T03:28:11.092Z","description":"ARM mbed TLS before 1.3.22, before 2.1.10, and before 2.7.0 allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary code or cause a denial of service (buffer overflow) via a crafted certificate chain that is mishandled during RSASSA-PSS signature verification within a TLS or DTLS session.","cwe":["buffer overflow"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"ARM mbed TLS before 1.3.22, before 2.1.10, and before 2.7.0","versions":["affected ARM mbed TLS before 1.3.22, before 2.1.10, and before 2.7.0"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2018/dsa-4147","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-4147"},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2018/dsa-4138","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-4138"},{"url":"https://tls.mbed.org/tech-updates/security-advisories/mbedtls-security-advisory-2018-01","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/103056","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"103056"},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/201804-19","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-201804-19"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/4267-1/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-4267-1"}],"vendors":["arm","crypto-libs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-0488","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"debian","published":"2018-02-13T15:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T03:28:11.050Z","description":"ARM mbed TLS before 1.3.22, before 2.1.10, and before 2.7.0, when the truncated HMAC extension and CBC are used, allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary code or cause a denial of service (heap corruption) via a crafted application packet within a TLS or DTLS session.","cwe":["heap corruption"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"ARM mbed TLS before 1.3.22, before 2.1.10, and before 2.7.0","versions":["affected ARM mbed TLS before 1.3.22, before 2.1.10, and before 2.7.0"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/103057","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"103057"},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2018/dsa-4147","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-4147"},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2018/dsa-4138","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-4138"},{"url":"https://tls.mbed.org/tech-updates/security-advisories/mbedtls-security-advisory-2018-01","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/201804-19","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-201804-19"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/4267-1/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-4267-1"}],"vendors":["arm","crypto-libs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-0497","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"debian","published":"2018-07-28T17:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T03:28:11.012Z","description":"ARM mbed TLS before 2.12.0, before 2.7.5, and before 2.1.14 allows remote attackers to achieve partial plaintext recovery (for a CBC based ciphersuite) via a timing-based side-channel attack. This vulnerability exists because of an incorrect fix (with a wrong SHA-384 calculation) for CVE-2013-0169.","cwe":["plaintext recovery"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"ARM mbed TLS before 2.12.0, before 2.7.5, and before 2.1.14","versions":["affected ARM mbed TLS before 2.12.0, before 2.7.5, and before 2.1.14"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2018/09/msg00029.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20180925 [SECURITY] [DLA 1518-1] polarssl security update"},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2018/dsa-4296","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-4296"},{"url":"https://tls.mbed.org/tech-updates/security-advisories/mbedtls-security-advisory-2018-02","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/4267-1/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-4267-1"}],"vendors":["arm","crypto-libs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-0498","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"debian","published":"2018-07-28T17:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T03:28:10.856Z","description":"ARM mbed TLS before 2.12.0, before 2.7.5, and before 2.1.14 allows local users to achieve partial plaintext recovery (for a CBC based ciphersuite) via a cache-based side-channel attack.","cwe":["plaintext recovery"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"ARM mbed TLS before 2.12.0, before 2.7.5, and before 2.1.14","versions":["affected ARM mbed TLS before 2.12.0, before 2.7.5, and before 2.1.14"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2018/09/msg00029.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20180925 [SECURITY] [DLA 1518-1] polarssl security update"},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2018/dsa-4296","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-4296"},{"url":"https://tls.mbed.org/tech-updates/security-advisories/mbedtls-security-advisory-2018-02","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/4267-1/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-4267-1"}],"vendors":["arm","crypto-libs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-5382","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"certcc","published":"2018-04-16T13:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-16T16:27:56.228Z","title":"Bouncy Castle BKS-V1 keystore files vulnerable to trivial hash collisions","description":"The default BKS keystore use an HMAC that is only 16 bits long, which can allow an attacker to compromise the integrity of a BKS keystore. Bouncy Castle release 1.47 changes the BKS format to a format which uses a 160 bit HMAC instead. This applies to any BKS keystore generated prior to BC 1.47. For situations where people need to create the files for legacy reasons a specific keystore type \"BKS-V1\" was introduced in 1.49. It should be noted that the use of \"BKS-V1\" is discouraged by the library authors and should only be used where it is otherwise safe to do so, as in where the use of a 16 bit checksum for the file integrity check is not going to cause a security issue in itself.","cwe":["CWE-327 CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"Legion of the Bouncy Castle","product":"Bouncy Castle","versions":["affected all <1.47 (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/103453","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"103453"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:2927","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:2927"},{"url":"https://www.kb.cert.org/vuls/id/306792","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_CERT-VN"],"name":"VU#306792"},{"url":"https://www.bouncycastle.org/releasenotes.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/security-alerts/cpuoct2020.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["crypto-libs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-8970","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2018-03-24T21:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T07:10:47.345Z","description":"The int_x509_param_set_hosts function in lib/libcrypto/x509/x509_vpm.c in LibreSSL 2.7.0 before 2.7.1 does not support a certain special case of a zero name length, which causes silent omission of hostname verification, and consequently allows man-in-the-middle attackers to spoof servers and obtain sensitive information via a crafted certificate. NOTE: the LibreSSL documentation indicates that this special case is supported, but the BoringSSL documentation does not.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/libressl-portable/openbsd/commit/0654414afcce51a16d35d05060190a3ec4618d42","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://ftp.openbsd.org/pub/OpenBSD/LibreSSL/libressl-2.7.1-relnotes.txt","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl/+/e759a9cd84198613199259dbed401f4951747cff","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["crypto-libs"]}
