{"id":"CVE-2018-12384","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mozilla","published":"2019-04-29T14:22:53.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T08:31:00.061Z","description":"When handling a SSLv2-compatible ClientHello request, the server doesn't generate a new random value but sends an all-zero value instead. This results in full malleability of the ClientHello for SSLv2 used for TLS 1.2 in all versions prior to NSS 3.39. This does not impact TLS 1.3.","cwe":["Use of Insufficiently Random Values"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"NSS","product":"Network Security Services (NSS)","versions":["affected All versions prior to NSS 3.39"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=CVE-2018-12384","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpuoct2019-5072832.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["crypto-libs","mozilla"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-12434","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2018-06-15T02:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-16T22:52:15.412Z","description":"LibreSSL before 2.6.5 and 2.7.x before 2.7.4 allows a memory-cache side-channel attack on DSA and ECDSA signatures, aka the Return Of the Hidden Number Problem or ROHNP. To discover a key, the attacker needs access to either the local machine or a different virtual machine on the same physical host.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://ftp.openbsd.org/pub/OpenBSD/LibreSSL/libressl-2.7.4-relnotes.txt","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://www.nccgroup.trust/us/our-research/technical-advisory-return-of-the-hidden-number-problem/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://ftp.openbsd.org/pub/OpenBSD/LibreSSL/libressl-2.6.5-relnotes.txt","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["crypto-libs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-12436","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2018-06-15T02:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-17T00:51:14.309Z","description":"wolfcrypt/src/ecc.c in wolfSSL before 3.15.1.patch allows a memory-cache side-channel attack on ECDSA signatures, aka the Return Of the Hidden Number Problem or ROHNP. To discover an ECDSA key, the attacker needs access to either the local machine or a different virtual machine on the same physical host.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://www.nccgroup.trust/us/our-research/technical-advisory-return-of-the-hidden-number-problem/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://www.wolfssl.com/wolfssh-and-rohnp/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/wolfSSL/wolfssl/commit/9b9568d500f31f964af26ba8d01e542e1f27e5ca","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["crypto-libs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-12440","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2018-06-15T02:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-16T20:37:40.252Z","description":"BoringSSL through 2018-06-14 allows a memory-cache side-channel attack on DSA signatures, aka the Return Of the Hidden Number Problem or ROHNP. To discover a DSA key, the attacker needs access to either the local machine or a different virtual machine on the same physical host.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://www.nccgroup.trust/us/our-research/technical-advisory-return-of-the-hidden-number-problem/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["crypto-libs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-16528","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2018-12-06T23:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T10:24:32.789Z","description":"Amazon Web Services (AWS) FreeRTOS through 1.3.1 allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary code because of mbedTLS context object corruption in prvSetupConnection and GGD_SecureConnect_Connect in AWS TLS connectivity modules.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/aws/amazon-freertos/blob/v1.3.2/CHANGELOG.md","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://blog.zimperium.com/freertos-tcpip-stack-vulnerabilities-details/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://blog.zimperium.com/freertos-tcpip-stack-vulnerabilities-put-wide-range-devices-risk-compromise-smart-homes-critical-infrastructure-systems/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["crypto-libs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-16868","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2018-12-03T14:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T10:32:54.146Z","description":"A Bleichenbacher type side-channel based padding oracle attack was found in the way gnutls handles verification of RSA decrypted PKCS#1 v1.5 data. An attacker who is able to run process on the same physical core as the victim process, could use this to extract plaintext or in some cases downgrade any TLS connections to a vulnerable server.","cwe":["CWE-203 CWE-203"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.0","score":4.7,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.0/AV:P/AC:H/PR:H/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:N/A:N"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"[UNKNOWN]","product":"gnutls","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/106080","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"106080"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2019-05/msg00017.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2019:1353"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2019-05/msg00068.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2019:1477"},{"url":"http://cat.eyalro.net/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=CVE-2018-16868","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["crypto-libs"]}
