{"id":"CVE-2018-1000520","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2018-06-26T16:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T12:40:47.241Z","description":"ARM mbedTLS version 2.7.0 and earlier contains a Ciphersuite Allows Incorrectly Signed Certificates vulnerability in mbedtls_ssl_get_verify_result() that can result in ECDSA-signed certificates are accepted, when only RSA-signed ones should be.. This attack appear to be exploitable via Peers negotiate a TLS-ECDH-RSA-* ciphersuite. Any of the peers can then provide an ECDSA-signed certificate, when only an RSA-signed one should be accepted..","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/ARMmbed/mbedtls/issues/1561","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["crypto-libs"]}
